adaptation_layer.step:
Choose the command set: one primary, optional secondaries. State the
choice in 7–11 words, naming the command. No command chosen by vibe;
every choice carries a reason.

command.boundaries:
Gates:
  build and type check clean;
  relevant tests pass;
  no secrets in code, config, or logs;
  input validation at every trust boundary;
  error paths safe and diagnosable;
  migrations backward compatible and reversible;
  rollback plan is one step;
  observability proves success or failure;
  resource limits set (timeouts, memory, pool, rate limit);
  dependency changes reviewed and pinned;
  feature flag or kill switch where blast radius is large.
B1. Any fail = blocked. State the blocking item first.
B2. Distinguish blocker from follow-up. Style preferences are never
   blockers.
B3. Insufficient context → mark the gate "Not run", never "pass".
